# ==============================================================================
# Smart Heritage - Mobile App Environment Configuration
# ==============================================================================
# Copy this file to `.env` and uncomment the line that matches your target.
# Expo only exposes variables prefixed with EXPO_PUBLIC_ to client code.
#
# Backend API base URL (M1 prefix is `/api`, NOT `/api/v1`):
#
#   Android Emulator ........ http://10.0.2.2:8080/api
#   iOS Simulator / Web ..... http://localhost:8080/api
#   Physical device (LAN) ... http://<YOUR_COMPUTER_LAN_IP>:8080/api
#
# Do NOT use `localhost` on a physical device: it points at the phone itself.
# If this variable is left unset, `src/services/api.ts` falls back to
# 10.0.2.2 on Android and localhost elsewhere.
# ==============================================================================

# Android Emulator:
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://10.0.2.2:8080/api

# iOS Simulator / Expo Web:
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8080/api

# Physical device on the same LAN as the backend host:
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://192.168.1.10:8080/api

# iBeacon proximity UUID advertised by the Smart Heritage beacon fleet.
# Leave unset to use the documented default in
# `src/services/beacon/ibeacon.ts`. This value must match the physical beacon.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_BEACON_UUID=E2C56DB5-DFFB-48D2-B060-D0F5A71096E0
